/P 736 0 R
/T (Inside the loop, we can use digitalWrite\(\) to turn an output ON or OFF. For example, digitalWrite\(ledPin, HIGH\); will turn the LED ON, and digitalWrite\(ledPin, LOW\); will turn it OFF. We can also use analogWrite\(\) to control the brightness of an LED or the speed of a motor using PWM. The value ranges from 0 \(off\) to 255 \(full brightness\), with values in between giving different levels.)
/E (Inside the loop, we can use digitalWrite\(\) to turn an output ON or OFF. For example, digitalWrite\(ledPin, HIGH\); will turn the LED ON, and digitalWrite\(ledPin, LOW\); will turn it OFF. We can also use analogWrite\(\) to control the brightness of an LED or the speed of a motor using PWM. The value ranges from 0 \(off\) to 255 \(full brightness\), with values in between giving different levels.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
