/Title (Next comes the setup\(\) function. This part runs only one time when the Arduino is turned on. It is used to prepare the pins and start things like the Serial Monitor. Inside setup, we use pinMode\(\) to tell the Arduino whether a pin will work as an input or an output. For example, setting a pin as OUTPUT allows it to control devices like an LED.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 1422 0 R
/Next 1426 0 R
>>
endobj
